From a8a34bdb8e775306f5d084a159e34e6b344a5247 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhruv Srivastav <dhruv08.srivastav@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:42:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Auto-pin on click-through, clearer unpin, honest credits
 section
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Opening a result now keeps it with the idea: the tiny Pin button was the
only way in, and it reads as debug UI below a wall of snippet text. The
click-through is the strongest signal of intent, so VisitLink fires a
fire-and-forget pinVisited() and the new tab opens without waiting. pin()
de-dupes, so re-opening a link changes nothing. The explicit Pin button
stays for keeping something without leaving the page, and a hint line says
what the click does — auto-pinning nobody knows about makes the export
untrustworthy.

Idea page: Remove -> Unpin, matching the vocabulary of the rest of the UI.

Print sheet: attributionRequired() answers true for UNKNOWN, which is right
for a badge but wrong for a credit line — there is no correct attribution
under an unidentified licence. Unknown-licence rows now get their own
'Licence unstated' section telling the user to confirm with the provider.
Fixed in the print page; lib/core stays frozen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRrqAosPMP4xAwyzKWyV5b
