From 2c865236e8da43f866719e8085971b2180361caa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dhruv Srivastav <dhruv08.srivastav@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:51:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Restructure the export sheet: abstracts, then links, then
 plates
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sheet now reads as a report rather than a dump. Each text source leads
with the provider's abstract and carries its link underneath, so the reader
meets the argument before the URL. Images collect at the end as plates, each
with its provider link and provenance below it — one partition of the pins by
kind, no per-row branching.

The sheet is also a preview now. Auto-print fired the dialog before anyone had
read anything; the page is what you read, and Save as PDF is the deliberate
next step, with a line saying the dialog's own Save as PDF is the destination.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QRrqAosPMP4xAwyzKWyV5b
